    <button class="btn-roll" id="newHandBtn">New Hand</button>
  </div>

  <div class="chip-strip">
    <span class="chip-label">Chip</span>
    <div id="chipSelector"></div>
  </div>

  <div class="table-actions">
    <button class="btn-outline" id="resetBtn">Reset Bankroll</button>
  </div>

  <div class="log" id="log"></div>

  <details class="legend">
    <summary>Rules &amp; payouts</summary>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Object</b> — bet on which hand, Player or Banker, will score closer to 9, or bet Tie. Cards 2-9 are face value, 10/J/Q/K count as 0, Aces count as 1. Hand value is the sum of both cards' values, keeping only the last digit (a 7 and an 8 make 15, which counts as 5).</li>
      <li><b>No decisions</b> — once your bet is down, the hand plays itself. Player and Banker each draw a third card automatically under a fixed set of rules; you just watch it resolve.</li>
      <li><b>Natural</b> — an 8 or 9 on the first two cards, for either hand, ends the round immediately with no third cards.</li>
      <li><b>Player bet</b> — pays {{ baccaratOdds.payoutStr.player }}. Pushes (bet returned) if the hands tie.</li>
      <li><b>Banker bet</b> — pays {{ baccaratOdds.payoutStr.banker }} minus a {{ baccaratOdds.bankerCommissionPct }}% commission on the win, charged only when Banker wins. Pushes if the hands tie.</li>
      <li><b>Tie bet</b> — pays {{ baccaratOdds.payoutStr.tie }}. Only a Tie bet wins on a tie; it's a separate bet from Player or Banker.</li>
      <li><b>Shoe</b> — dealt from a real 8-deck shoe, reshuffled between hands once it runs low.</li>
    </ul>
  </details>

  <p>
    Baccarat is a comparing game between two hands, Player and Banker — the names
    don't refer to you or the house, they're just the two hands' labels. There are
    no strategic decisions once you've placed your bet: every third-card draw
    follows a fixed rule, so the entire game comes down to picking which of the
    three bets to make.
  </p>
